+# Agent Note: File-tree drags insert composer references
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-12-workspace-file-tree-drag-references.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The right Sidebar exposes workspace files and the composer accepts operating-system file drops, but dragging a file row from the Sidebar into the composer has no transferable identity. Treating that gesture as a byte upload would duplicate a file already governed by the Session workspace, hide later workspace edits behind an uploaded copy, and bypass the existing structured file-reference path.
+
+## Decision
+
+File rows publish their existing Session-scoped `dsh-resource://file` address under a dedicated `DataTransfer` type. The shared attachment drop target recognizes that type in addition to browser `Files` and forwards the address to the composer owner. Browser `Files` retain the existing attachment-intake path.
+
+The composer accepts only non-empty, relative file addresses owned by its current Session. It converts an accepted address into the same atomic reference chip produced by the file-reference source and inserts it over the live editor selection. Foreign-Session addresses, external URLs, absolute paths, locked composers, and composers without attachment intake are ignored.
+
+The transfer carries a resource address instead of serialized file bytes or untrusted display text. The existing reference codec therefore remains responsible for clipboard text, submission text, Session logging, reload projection, and model-visible file resolution.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Upload the workspace file as an attachment.** Rejected because the source already belongs to the Session workspace. Uploading creates a second byte identity and changes the gesture from “reference this file” to “copy this version of the file.”
+
+**Use `text/plain` or `text/uri-list`.** Rejected because unrelated browser and application drags commonly populate those formats. A product-specific type identifies the intended internal gesture; the composer still parses and validates its resource address.
+
+**Pass a workspace path directly between the Sidebar and conversation packages.** Rejected because the resource address already carries the Session scope needed to prevent cross-Session insertion and is the file viewer's established identity.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Dragging a workspace file inserts a structured reference at the current selection and shows the existing full-page drop affordance. Clicking the same row still opens the file preview. Directories remain click-only. Unit tests cover transfer production, drop routing, reference conversion, and rejection cases; the real Web composition drags a nested workspace row into the resident composer.
